 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? That's lovely. You don't need to speak the language yourself. Set an example by reading to her in English, and listen when she reads in French. She would. Offer to come in for a trial session, or help her prepare for tests. French parents value interaction over knowledge, so being there is the biggest gift. She might, at first. Show her your support by asking about her day, and asking her to practice with you. Most little ones love neat little language games. There are few song lyrics you can sing together, and simple rhyming books are great for young readers. You' supporting her without overwhelming yourself. That's the key.",
